<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil soars, supply very tight.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil soars, supply very tight.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5107)  DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     38.80/38.90     25.68/25.75     38.10/38.40</p>
<p> BREMEN		38.80/38.90     25.68/25.75     38.10/38.40</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    39.50/39.70     26.15/26.28     38.90/39.20</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   40.70/40.90     26.94/27.07     40.30/40.60</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   41.00/41.10     27.14/27.21     40.50/40.80</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  42.40/42.70     28.07/28.27     42.10/42.50</p>
<p>German inland gas oil rose again on Wednesday with IPE futures and Rotterdam markets, but freight rates fell from their recent highs, suppliers said. One said the barging to Karlsruhe fell from 28.50 dm/l to 26.00 dm. -- Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
